  <section id="dining">
    <h2>Dining</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>'Ohana</strong> is the family-style restaurant. Breakfast is the Best Friends Breakfast featuring Lilo &amp; Stitch, listed at 7:30 a.m. to 12:15 p.m. when we checked. Dinner is Hawaiian-flavored and served family-style, 3:30 p.m. to 10:00 p.m. Characters do not come out at dinner. <span class="verify">[verify hours still current]</span></li>
      <li><strong>Kona Cafe</strong> is table service for breakfast, lunch and dinner, with an onstage sushi kitchen. Disney listed breakfast 7:30 a.m. to 11:00 a.m., lunch 11:45 a.m. to 2:00 p.m., and dinner 5:00 p.m. to 10:00 p.m. <span class="verify">[verify hours still current]</span></li>
      <li><strong>Capt. Cook's</strong> and <strong>Chip 'n' Dale's Deli</strong> are the quick-service restaurants.</li>
      <li><strong>Pineapple Lanai</strong> is the walk-up window for pineapple soft-serve and snacks.</li>
      <li><strong>Trader Sam's Grog Grotto</strong> is the themed bar. <strong>Tambu Lounge</strong> sits near 'Ohana. <strong>Kona Island</strong> is a smaller cafe and sushi counter. <strong>Barefoot Pool Bar</strong> is at the Lava Pool, and <strong>Oasis Bar &amp; Grill</strong> is at the Oasis Pool.</li>
      <li>You can use mobile ordering in the My Disney Experience app at the quick-service spots.</li>
      <li><strong>Park dining reservations:</strong> Disney resort guests can book their whole stay (up to 10 nights) starting 60 days before arrival. 'Ohana books up, so plan ahead.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: your go-to meal here, and one thing you'd skip.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="pools">
    <h2>Pools and things to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lava Pool</strong> is the main pool. It has a volcano, a waterfall, a 142-foot slide and a zero-depth entry, with a lounge and bar nearby. This is the busy one.</li>
      <li><strong>Oasis Pool</strong> is a quieter, all-ages leisure pool in a garden. You can rent an Oasis Patio, a private shaded area for up to six people, first-come or by calling Disney. Food and drinks can be delivered from Oasis Bar &amp; Grill.</li>
      <li><strong>Cove Pool</strong> is a zero-entry pool at Island Tower. Official listings say Polynesian Village guests can use it. <strong>Moana's Voyage</strong>, also at Island Tower, is a splash area for little kids.</li>
      <li>Towels are free at the pools. Hours and lifeguard coverage vary and can change.</li>
    </ul>
