  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Start with a Resort View room if the view is not the point.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran from $771 to $1,371 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates. That is the lowest hotel rate at this resort.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay more for Water View or Theme Park View only if you will use it.</strong> Water View rooms ran about $876 to $1,446. Theme Park View was higher still. Confirm the view you are buying, especially if exterior work is still affecting lagoon sightlines.</li>
      <li><strong>Club Level is a different product.</strong> You are paying for the lounge, not just a nicer view. Compare that cost with eating some of those meals at Kona Cafe or Capt. Cook's.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more.</strong> Deluxe rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $35 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="fg-callout">
      <h3>Rates change</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">The rate range above is MouseSavers' October 2026 snapshot of Disney's full prices, not a deal. Always check the live price on Disney's site before you book.</p>
    </div>
